WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.365
Follow the instruction path across the top.

2
00:00:03.365 --> 00:00:10.253
The frontend selects fetch addresses and uses branch prediction to help maintain supply.

3
00:00:10.253 --> 00:00:13.618
Decode identifies operations and registers.

4
00:00:13.618 --> 00:00:17.845
Issue checks operand and execution-resource readiness,

5
00:00:17.845 --> 00:00:22.463
while the scoreboard tracks instructions and their results.

6
00:00:22.463 --> 00:00:27.707
Execution handles integer operations, branches and memory accesses,

7
00:00:27.707 --> 00:00:30.524
returning results to the scoreboard.

8
00:00:30.524 --> 00:00:35.690
Floating-point and coprocessor interfaces depend on configuration;

9
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.994
the coprocessor itself is not built into every variant.

10
00:00:39.994 --> 00:00:46.647
Commit then updates architectural registers and CSRs in program order and coordinates

11
00:00:46.647 --> 00:00:49.073
relevant stores and exceptions.

12
00:00:49.073 --> 00:00:54.787
Outside the core, the platform supplies memory, interconnect, interrupts,

13
00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.509
debug and peripherals.

14
00:00:56.509 --> 00:01:02.144
Fetching instructions and loading program data create different traffic,

15
00:01:02.144 --> 00:01:06.762
using the selected memory support and platform connections.

16
00:01:06.762 --> 00:01:11.223
Debug is not the destination of an ordinary data request.

17
00:01:11.223 --> 00:01:15.136
Cache, translation and bus details are simplified,

18
00:01:15.136 --> 00:01:20.067
and crossed lines without a junction do not denote connections.

19
00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:24.841
This is a responsibility diagram, not a complete RTL netlist.

20
00:01:24.841 --> 00:01:30.164
The historical six-stage description refers to an original baseline;

21
00:01:30.164 --> 00:01:33.686
box counts specify neither stages nor cycles.

22
00:01:33.686 --> 00:01:40.260
Next, two instructions make the distinction between waiting and committing concrete.

